      "value": "@{60285ca04963ba22994f485b|full_name}: okay, I think I understand this better now. On Start I was trying to take ownership of a bunch of tiles (probably bad) and some internal state was getting out of sync.\nHowever! It does seem that it's failing to receive some subset of tile data on initial join sync, perhaps because it's confused about whether it owns things. That is, some subset of tiles end up in a state where both sides think they own and have serialized data.\nSince this involves attempts to RequestSerialization and TakeOwnership in Start I'm not sure this is a bug in UNU, but it was certainly tricky to track down.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
