  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When there is heavy transmit activity on a single frame, manually synced events can be dropped without retransmitting.\nI've been unable to create a _minimal_ repro thus far, but I do have a consistent repro world for you at least: wrld_ca2bb56a-19c1-4ef5-8ef6-d060ae9fd8b0\nRepro steps:\n1. Connect two clients. In each, click the big vase next to the pens to enable world debugging options.\n2. Click the shuffle button on either client and wait for shuffle to finish\n3. Now, click the 'tile state histograms' button on the debug panel on both. The 'synced' values that appear should be the same (but, due to this bug, sometimes aren't). These directly measure the number of manually synced objects with a particular value for a synced state variable.\n4. Click 'reveal tiles' on non-master to trigger another flurry of activity, then perform the histograms check on both again. The correct behaviour is for all of the synced variables to go to state 5, but in fact, on the master only about 100 change to 5, and the rest remain as they were.\nVideo of repro procedure: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fy3SG2qRTzo\nThis does not repro every time, but it seems to happen more than half the time for me. When it occurs, it seems that often, exactly 100 manually-synced objects are transmitted (and the rest remain unsynced until the next RequestSerialization), suggesting there might be an undocumented limit of some sort here.\nIf you're examining this in the editor, the objects in question are named \"ManualSync\" and each have a single synced int.",
